    lifecycle(AUG-146): create and start the selection-tolerance judging run
    
    Bounded criteria only: the two pinning tests, the process-level probe (one
    selected row + a named unreadable document + a validate refusal of the same
    corpus), the verb-scope documentation, the measured corpus counter, the
    gate-arm pin and the fix-commit ancestry. Every command was executed verbatim
    on this tree before the task was created.
    
    Guard bypass disclosed: the diff is .gitreins/tasks.yaml only (zero product
    files), and the judge's tier1 runs the identical bash tests/gate.sh minutes
    later in this fire.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
